Chapter 10: "The Kingdom of the Lion King"
Chapter 10-22: "Preparatory Moves and Refusal"

---

—This occurred at the same time Natsuki Subaru, in the "Six Tongues" hideout, was told about the dreadnought-class calamity afflicting the Kingdom of Lugunica; a scene in the commercial district of the Royal Capital of Lugunica.

---

"—By some means or another, the enemy has already seized the Dragon History Stone and taken complete control. That is the situation the Royal Castle finds itself in now. I've filled in the gaps in the information with my own speculation, but I doubt I'm far off the mark."

"...Indeed. It would also explain why we're being hounded right now. At the very least, we should consider the chain of command at the Royal Castle to be under their control."

"— —"

"Garfiel, are you alright?"

"Eh? O-Oh, I'm fine... Nah, honestly, talk's on a scale I never even thought about, so... I just dunno what to say."

Shaking his head, Garfiel revealed his all-too-honest feelings. But Otto empathized with his younger brother-in-arms, knowing it couldn't be helped.

"...Given the situation, after all."

To be frank, Otto himself was equally plagued by confusion and bewilderment. The only difference was their roles within the camp; Otto was simply not allowed to stop thinking.

In this dire situation, Garfiel had done his duty well. —No, it wasn't just Garfiel. It was the result of everyone working together as one, giving it their all.
The only one who failed was himself, who had his weapon taken away so pathetically.

"—Tch."

Leaning against the wall, sitting with one knee drawn up, Garfiel groaned in pain from his throat.
The deep exhaustion and pain that wouldn't fade from his face was unthinkable for Garfiel, who possessed extraordinary toughness and recovery power. It spoke to just how extraordinary and absurd the power of the one who landed that blow on him—Reinhard—truly was.

—It had been some time since Reinhard had stood in Otto's way, and they had barely managed to break through using every card they had.

The battle had lasted less than a minute, but by the end, everyone was battered and bruised. Garfiel, who had engaged Reinhard in a direct confrontation, was in a particularly terrible state. Otto felt pathetic; even after deliberately luring the enemy into carelessness, he was incapacitated just from a blow grazing his chin.

The victory they had somehow scraped together—and it was only thanks to unexpected reinforcements—and the fact that they were even brought to that situation in the first place, left Otto with far too much to reflect on.
The only reason they could even have something resembling a debriefing was because the reinforcements who met up with them had led them here, securing them a momentary safe haven.

"—Just managing to shake that one off is a feat in itself. Even if it was a role forced upon him, a hundred ordinary soldiers wouldn't be able to lay a finger on him."

"But, for that, we had to make her play a card she shouldn't have had to play. What she was forced to let go from her life is significant. I cannot forgive that person."

"...Your indignation is likely justified. I'm sure he's prepared to be resented. That is what it means to be the 'Sword Saint'. I myself have never lost my anger towards the 'Sword Saint'."

"That is..."

Otto narrowed his eyes quietly at the man who placed a large hand on his own bald head.
What he was about to say—whether a question or speculation—he bit his tongue, aware that he had already let slip something he shouldn't have.

However—

"—You are speaking of anger towards my wife, not Reinhard, aren't you."

Instead of Otto, who had fallen silent, the old swordsman—Wilhelm—entered through the door and took those words with a tone of certainty.

Wilhelm came into the room, bringing Rem and an elderly man with short hair with him. He first let Rem inside, then turned to the man,

"Conwood, I'm sorry for the trouble. I'm in your debt for hiding us."

"Hah, to have Wilhelm Trias—the man who was the very embodiment of arrogance and selfishness—thank me so admirably... It might just rain tomorrow."

"You..."

"It's a joke. —And besides, it's only natural. It's the natural thing to do, Wilhelm. Me lending you my strength... that's a given, no need for thanks."

"— —"

After the familiar tone, the man’s voice trembled, and Wilhelm's cheeks stiffened.
The man relaxed his cheeks, seeming to find his old friend's reaction amusing, then looked at Otto and Garfiel inside the room.

"I owe a debt to your comrade, Natsuki Subaru-dono, from the White Whale hunt. A debt so huge it'd take a lifetime to repay. I won't let anyone through here, so rest easy."

"...Shopkeeper, you have my gratitude."

"I told you. My gratitude is far greater. ...No one believes Natsuki Subaru-dono is part of the Witch's Cult. It's the same with Crusch-sama."

Saying that, the man clapped Wilhelm on the shoulder and left the room, closing the door. Watching his back disappear behind the door, Otto called out, "Rem-san."

The place they had reached, guided by Wilhelm, was a private room in a tavern offered as a shelter. While Otto and the others explained the situation in this room, Rem had been in a separate room.
The reason was—

"Are Petra-chan and the others alright?"

"...For now, they're resting. Petra-chan was quite distraught, and Meili-chan ended up being the one to soothe her... but they've both fallen asleep."

"I see... Understood. Thank you."

"No, I didn't do anything. More importantly, what about the discussion?"

"—We've just finished confirming the current situation, I suppose."

Otto directed his pale blue eyes to the back of the room and answered a tense-looking Rem.
Following her gaze, there stood a large figure, seated in a private room chair yet still with his head higher than Otto or Wilhelm.

A giant of advanced age with a bald head and sun-darkened skin, his name was—

"—Barga Cromwell. Formerly one of the primary figures who escalated the kingdom's civil war."

"...Unfortunately, I have no idea who you're talking about. I'm just Old Man Rom, an oversized geezer living in the slums, nothing more."

"How brazen. What about the scar on my chest that I gouged out? Are you hiding it under that great bushy white chest hair of yours?"

"I have even less idea what you mean. Not that it concerns me, but I'd rather not get old. To think even the renowned 'Sword Demon' can't match the passage of years with his wits."

"You bastard—"

"...Both of you, please stop fighting. Petra-chan and the others are resting upstairs. Don't we have no time for infighting?"

Rem stepped forward, as if cutting between the two at odds, and glared at them alternately. Faced with her stern gaze, Wilhelm bowed his head, and the giant figure—the old giant who called himself Old Man Rom—also cleared his throat and showed an attitude of compliance towards Rem.

While grateful for Rem's intervention and judgment, Otto couldn't help but feel a certain sense of understanding regarding the hostile exchange between those two.

—Otto was also a citizen of this Dragonfriend Kingdom of Lugunica.
He knew the facts: 'Sword Demon' Wilhelm van Astrea was a hero of the 'Demi-Human War', and Barga Cromwell was one of those who commanded the Demi-Human Alliance during that civil war.

He never imagined that Barga Cromwell was still alive.
Of course, the man himself—Old Man Rom—denied any connection to Barga, and would likely never admit it.

At any rate—

"I'll call you Rom-san... Thank you for sending Wilhelm-san as reinforcements. Without that, we would have been annihilated by now."

"I doubt you could call that an exaggeration. In your current state, if you were captured by the castle—not being a royal selection candidate or a knight—they could make you disappear however they like and cover it up."

"Make us disappear, how could they..."

"We must consider the worst possibilities. Even if we dislike it and flee to optimism, there's no reason the enemy would go easy on us. ...Especially now that Miklotov is dead."

Rem was at a loss for words at Old Man Rom's grave assessment, but Otto agreed.
Always assume the worst. Ultimately, that's what leads to finding a way out of a desperate situation. Even he himself thinks it’s pessimism.

"Yo, Wilhelm-san, you saved my ass earlier."

At that moment, Garfiel, sitting against the wall, raised a hand lightly towards Wilhelm. At his call, Wilhelm turned, "Garfiel-dono,"

"In that situation, my skill was insufficient; my apologies. I had to surprise him by aiming to cut you as well, otherwise I could not have reached Reinhard with my sword."

"That was somethin' I was ready for when I took it on, so no worries. That wound's already mostly closed up. ...The 'Sword Saint's' hand strike, though... still nowhere near healed."

"— —"

"More 'mportantly, what were ya doin', Wilhelm-san? I hear our boss 'n that Duchess were escapin' together..."

"Indeed. Let me tell you what happened on my side."

With that, Wilhelm began to calmly recount the circumstances surrounding himself and his master, Crusch.

"After Subaru-dono and Emilia-sama visited the mansion and departed, Crusch-sama, having seen them off, secluded herself in her room. Of course, none of the household, myself included, could approach her, and she was not even taking proper meals."

"That must have been... worrying."

"Indeed. Everyone knew things couldn't continue that way. So, I left the mansion to prepare for requesting assistance from Crusch-sama's father, the former Duke, Meckart Karsten-sama. However, during my absence—"

"—Crusch-sama left the mansion alone and headed for the residence of Lord Miklotov McMahon."

"That's correct. By the time word reached my ears, it was already too late."

With an expression of deep regret, Wilhelm lamented his own inadequacy.
But if Crusch had deliberately waited for Wilhelm's absence, it was only a matter of sooner or later, and there was no reason he should be blamed.
Though, given the resulting situation, the 'Sword Demon's' self-reproach was understandable.

"Naturally, it is unthinkable that Crusch-sama would commit such a reckless act. I immediately went up to the Royal Castle and appealed to an old acquaintance, Lord Bordeaux Zellgef. However, not only would he not listen, but on my way back, I ended up being pursued by soldiers. That's when—"

"—I called out to him. Frankly, it was a bitter choice for me as well."

"...It was also not my intention to cut down Kingdom soldiers by force and break through. When I saw this man in a lit place, I doubted my own eyes."

"Both of you."

The inerasable anger and old grudges inevitably laced their words with venom.
While watching the men being gently rebuked by Rem, Otto understood the circumstances of their meeting. And how Wilhelm came to join them.

"That being the case, what about you, Rom-san? It seems you were remarkably well-prepared, or rather, quick to act."

"It's natural for you to be suspicious, but I was only able to move just before things happened, much like yourselves. I only noticed because my nose is sharp... Since long ago, I've had a sense for approaching danger. It's been rusty for a while, but the recent turmoil seems to have knocked the rust off."

"I see. —Understood."

Otto didn't press further on Old Man Rom, who rolled his large shoulders and answered matter-of-factly.
Ultimately, they were only facing the same direction at this moment; their positions were fundamentally opposed. It was only natural for him to keep his cards hidden, and to blame him for it would be narrow-minded.

At the very least, Old Man Rom's actions had saved Otto and the others from a pinch. For now, appreciating that action should take precedence over doubting his true intentions.

"You're a scary young man. Your eyes aren't smiling at all."

"Sorry. Merchants are supposed to smile in public and chuckle inwardly in private, but lately, I've had trouble acting very merchant-like. Even I find it distasteful. —Though, if being a good-natured merchant means letting one's own people die, then such a person is unnecessary right now."

"— —"

"...Sorry, I spoke out of turn."

After shrugging and replying, Otto chastised himself for the unnecessary words.
Keeping it to his thoughts was one thing, but once spoken, words are as good as a weapon. If one suddenly draws a weapon while facing someone, they can't complain about being stabbed repeatedly.

As he suspected, being overcome in his 'Divine Protection of Word Soul' was affecting him more than he realized. He had always warned himself, like a curse, that entrusting his identity to his Divine Protection was dangerous, but recently he had relied on it too much. This was the price.

"—Anyway, our positions here are the same. Our masters have been unjustly defamed, and the Royal Castle tacitly approves... no, is actively leading it. The objective is to eliminate the royal selection candidates, destroy the very rules of the royal selection, and rule the kingdom."

"And for that, Emilia-san and that person are being slandered... The ones Wilhelm-san and Rom-san support are, too, is that it?"

"Emilia-sama, Felt-sama, and the Duchess... that means the only ones left are Anastasia-sama and the Church's new candidate, Feltore-sama."

"I wonder about that. If the 'Sage Council' and the participants of the half-round table are unscrupulous, there are any number of ways to defame Anastasia-sama. Since Anastasia-sama is from Kararagi, they could say she's plotting to have the city-state invade the Kingdom... Or perhaps, that she colluded with Emilia-sama in the Vollachia Empire to assassinate Priscilla-sama—"

"—Enough! Don't joke about that!"

At Otto's prediction of vicious scenarios, Rem raised her voice in anger.
Her pale blue eyes moist, breathing heavily, she clenched her fists tightly, enraged at the slanderous talk of Priscilla's death that Otto had speculated on.

"I will absolutely not allow Priscilla-san's, that person's death to be defiled and used! If they seriously say such things, I will not forgive it...! If it reaches Abel-san's ears, it will be war with Vollachia!"

"In reality, it's no laughing matter. Coldly treating Emilia-sama, who brought back results that could lead to a friendship treaty with the Empire, is tantamount to throwing mud in the face of the Empire that recognized Emilia-sama. It's a foolish reason for war, but history is full of foolish reasons for starting wars. And besides..."

"—Even if it comes to war, Reinhard is there. Controlling the Royal Castle means being able to move the 'Sword Saint'. Until now, the authority to issue orders to the 'Sword Saint' seems to have been strictly controlled to prevent that... but the enemy has gotten their hands on it."

"That can't... be..."

Though it was truly the worst possibility, Old Man Rom didn't deny Otto's thoughts, and instead paved over the nightmare by filling in the missing parts.
The horror was so great that Rem and Garfiel, who had just risked their lives to evade a single bout with Reinhard, were speechless.

Only one person—

"—So it is the 'Divine Protection of the Sword Saint' after all."

—The 'Sword Demon' muttered at a volume almost no one could hear.

"...Judging from the situation, the enemy clearly intends to attack the royal selection. That being the case, we must consider Filtore-sama, who recently appeared on the stage, and the 'Dragon Church' that supports her, to be on the enemy's side. Just to confirm, regarding the princess who disappeared fifteen years ago—"

"—Felt is Felt. There is no other answer."

Hating how the silence was stagnating the discussion, Otto tried to organize the situation and confirm facts, but Old Man Rom's words cut him off hard and clear.
As if realizing that a simple denial overlaying a question was unfriendly, Old Man Rom added, "However," to the surrounding eyes,

"The story that the 'Dragon Church' was sheltering the missing princess seems dubious at best. Even if they kept their distance from the Royal Castle, staying silent about that fact for over a year since the royal selection started... in the face of a crisis threatening the kingdom's very existence, that's unthinkable."

Balancing a firm opinion with an uncertain attitude, Old Man Rom was clearly hiding something.
Naturally, the sharpness in the 'Sword Demon's' eyes directed at the old giant intensified.

"— —"

Wilhelm, who had been the commander of the Royal Guard fifteen years ago, was also said to have been the person in charge of searching for the missing princess. His desire to know the truth about the princess suspicions cast on Felt and Filtore this time must have been stronger than anyone's.
However, the mental fortitude of the man suspected of being one of the three great heads of the Demi-Human Alliance was not so weak as to crack under the obsession dwelling in that gaze.

At any rate—

"...I understand how bad the situation is."

Exhaling a small breath, Rem straightened her back firmly, as if forcing a change of mood. She then looked around the room at the faces of Otto and the others,

"Frankly, I'm very worried about that person who isn't here, but Emilia-san and Sister in the castle are in danger, right? How on earth do we get those two... no, Felt-san as well. How do we get them out?"

"With Reinhard and the Knight Commander over there, a frontal assault's way too reckless no matter how ya look at it. It'd be like 'Gaddogi Guaddo Zeadd's Mountain Retreat'. We need a plan, Otto-nii."

Garfiel, heavily burdened from the fight with Reinhard, agreed with Rem and looked to Otto with eyes expecting a plan.
Both of them were undoubtedly worried about Emilia confined in the castle, and even more so about Ram, who accompanied her as her attendant.
It was truly heartbreaking to tell them this, but—

"—No. We will prioritize escaping from the Royal Capital. We don't have the leeway to extract Emilia-sama and Ram-san, or Felt-sama, from the Royal Castle."

"Wha—!?"

Eyes widening in shock, Garfiel and Rem raised their voices simultaneously. Garfiel put a hand on the wall and stood up, barking, "Otto-nii!"

"Escape... Ya mean we ain't goin' to help 'em?! What's that supposed to mean!"

"It means exactly what I said. Currently, we have neither the means nor the fighting strength to extract Emilia-sama and the others who are imprisoned in the castle. Any half-baked plan would be crushed by force, and we would all simply fall into enemy hands together. We cannot afford such a losing battle."

"A losing battle... But, Sister and Emilia-san are there..."

"I understand. But even if the enemy has already seized the Royal Castle, they cannot easily lay a hand on the royal selection candidates. Even Reinhard-san, who is their puppet, wouldn't be able to overlook such a move. Their freedom will be restricted, but as long as they are in the castle, there's a high possibility that Emilia-sama and the others won't be harmed. That's my assessment."

"B-But still..."

While Otto remained as calm as possible, careful not to let emotion into his voice, Garfiel and Rem, their feelings exposed, were greatly agitated. However, Old Man Rom raised a large hand and interjected into their exchange, "May I?"

"I agree with that youngster. Even if they're in the castle, I'll find a way to manage things with Felt and the others. What's scarier is giving them an excuse by our own actions. Their position has already worsened with that mabeast incident. We'd like to avoid making it worse if we can."

"Even you, Old Man Rom, agree with Otto-san? ...What about you, Wilhelm-san?"

"—I understand your feelings, Rem-dono, being worried about your master and sister. However, challenging a fully prepared opponent while resigned to disadvantage is a fool's errand... It vexes me, but Barga has a point."

At Wilhelm's answer, slowly shaking his head, Rem bit her lip.
Her frustration was painfully clear to Otto. Moreover, there was something Otto was deliberately not saying, to avoid further opposition from Rem and Garfiel.

Even if the 'Sage Council' has fallen into enemy hands, they cannot harm the royal selection candidates. —But that doesn't guarantee the safety of their attendants.
And, Ram, who volunteered to be the attendant, had been prepared for that possibility from the start, which is why she didn't yield that position to Rem or Petra.

"...Otto-nii, ya talk about leavin' the capital, but what about the boss and the others?"

"—Meeting up with them will be difficult. My Divine Protection is unreliable right now. If I talk to the wrong person carelessly, our internal situation will be laid bare. We can't take that risk."

If his 'Divine Protection of Word Soul' were in perfect condition, he could have searched for Subaru and the others by relying on numbers, or sent messages and notified them of a meeting place.
Now that that option was taken away, finding Subaru and the others without a lead was impossible.

"Barga, I won't press deeply. But you, surely you could find Crusch-sama and Subaru-dono..."

"You seem to think highly of a mere old geezer from the slums, but unfortunately, I can't live up to those expectations. I'm not being pretentious or holding back. The fragile thread has already frayed. I don't have any prospect of tying it back together."

"Useless when it really counts... No, I suppose I'm no different."

Wilhelm reflexively started to snap back, but hesitated through self-reflection. In Old Man Rom's eyes, glancing at him, there was a frustration suggesting those words weren't a lie.

Still, there were no moves to make. Faced with this situation, Rem tightly gripped the hem of her skirt.

"I can believe in Sister and the others in the castle. I feel that we here, if we combine our strength, can manage. But that person alone... he will definitely do something reckless. I know it."

"Rem..."

"No, I'm not the only one. Garf, Otto-san, you know too, don't you? At times like this, that person absolutely tries to do more than he can handle. And that will surely lead to him getting terribly hurt again. And yet..."

We can't be by his side. As Rem's words, soaked with heartfelt regret, lingered, no one could say anything.
It was surely because everyone here had been involved with Subaru in some way, had been saved by his actions exactly as Rem described, and had witnessed him getting hurt.

"...We'll be putting a burden on Beatrice-chan."

Now, the only hope for the entire camp was that Beatrice, the only one likely with Subaru, would function as a safety net for him. —As Otto and the others thought this, "No," Wilhelm stepped forward.
He stood before the downcast Rem, gently placing a hand on her shoulder,

"It's only natural to worry. But Subaru-dono is not alone with just Beatrice-dono. Crusch-sama is with them."

"—. But the prevailing rumor is that the Duchess has lost her mind. In fact, didn't she slip out of the mansion right under your nose?"

"Silence, Barga. What could you possibly understand about that person?"

"— —"

"It may be as you say, that I was deceived. But I believe Crusch-sama had something in mind. Until I hear it from her own lips, I will not arbitrarily jump to conclusions."

It wasn't just trading insults; Wilhelm's voice carried a solid core of conviction. With his blue eyes harboring loyalty to his absent master, he looked over Rem and everyone in the room.

"Even if her memories were stolen, the righteousness of her heart remains intact. It's not merely because of a debt regarding my wife. —I have decided, with all my heart and soul, to put that person on the throne."

"Wilhelm-san..."

"Crusch-sama is there. Subaru-dono is a man of his own caliber. And Beatrice-dono, when she's with Subaru-dono, she appears like a sweet, innocent child, but I've heard she is a Great Spirit who has lived for many long years. They will surely overcome our concerns."

The words he slowly spun were not just to persuade Rem, but more like forcefully scrawling his own wish upon the world, demanding it be so.
It even felt like a kind of arrogance, but when the 'Sword Demon'—who had once defeated the 'Sword Saint' himself and achieved his marriage by snatching his wife from fate—said it, it carried the persuasive power to believe it would be so.
An inexplicable power that made one think it might actually come true.

And that—

"...That's the kinda thing the boss would say."

"If so, that's a most honorable assessment."

When Garfiel voiced what Otto was also feeling, Wilhelm nodded deeply. Bathed up close in the 'Sword Demon's' appeal, Rem let the tension drain from her shoulders.
Her eyes and expression still held anxiety, but Rem bravely lifted her face nonetheless,

"Sorry, I lost my composure. You're right. If Beatrice-chan and Karsten-san are reliable, then one or two of his reckless acts... Will it really stop at just one or two?"

"You were almost convinced just now, so isn't it bad to get stuck on that point...?"

"Three or four, Beatrice'll manage somehow! ...Right now, believin' that's what we can do."

Saying that, even though his own anxiety hadn't been fully dispelled, Garfiel hid it and bared his fangs, to which Rem responded with a thin smile.
Otto, too. No one can act in this situation with all their anxieties resolved. They might later regret today's choices if an unwanted outcome appears.
Even so, they had no choice but to choose, so that they could step past this moment's hesitation.

"Then, once again—we will withdraw from the Royal Capital."

Clearing his throat, Otto looked around at everyone in the room and declared their policy once more.

The Royal Castle had already fallen into enemy hands, and they themselves had become wanted fugitives targeted by the capital's soldiers. If they moved carelessly, the 'Sword Saint' would be sent after them; if caught, their lives would be in danger—a truly desperate situation.
Leaving the Royal Capital in such a state would naturally be seen as tucking tail and running.

However, he would dare to say it.

"This is by no means a defeat. —It is a preparatory move, to ensure that next time, we will definitely strike back and win."

"Heh! That's just like ya, Otto-nii, a blood-boilin' declaration!"

"I'm not entirely satisfied with that assessment, you know!"

Among the nodding faces, Otto responded loudly to Garfiel, who rubbed his nose with his finger. Then, after nodding towards Rem, he turned his mind to the Royal Capital outside the walls.

He didn't know where they were. But he thought of Subaru and Beatrice, who, just like Otto and the others, were likely struggling in a dead end somewhere in this Royal Capital.
His worries were endless. Because, as Rem said, he would surely do something reckless.

—He didn't want him to. That was Otto's true feeling.

"...Even so, you're going to be reckless anyway, aren't you."

Letting the walls swallow his unvoiced murmur, Otto pulled his hat down low over his eyes.
Otto knew all too well that Natsuki Subaru would casually throw his life and heart onto the scales if it meant answering someone's expectations or wishes.
That's why, truly, he didn't want to rely on him, and he shouldn't rely on him.

Because he felt that counting on Natsuki Subaru as "the person who will do something," just like everyone else did, was tantamount to preying on his kindness and weakness.

So, so at the very least.
So that recklessness doesn't consume Natsuki Subaru and crush him.
Otto thought with a bitter feeling that even in a faraway place, they would do what they must to resist this unreasonableness and absurdity.

---

△▼△▼△▼△

---

"Achoo!"

"Did your body get cold? Are you alright, I wonder?"

"Nah, my nose just suddenly tickled. ...Though, I did feel a chill."

Subaru, who had sneezed from the sudden impulse deep in his nose, relaxed his lips at a worried Beatrice, but then couldn't even maintain a wry smile and sighed.
That was how shocking the story he'd heard from Russell was—the machinations of Capella of 'Lust' and the dire situation the Kingdom of Lugunica was in.

"A shapeshifter being troublesome is a classic trope, but... this bad, huh? No wonder you've been harassing Russell-san and the others for thirty years."

"To be precise, it was the Kingdom being harassed, and we were trying to stop it. Though, given our current pathetic state, I can't say that with much pride."

"We understand that you were holding the line at the water's edge. But there's something I can't wrap my head around. Why did that thirty-year tug-of-war suddenly tip?"

"That is... probably because of us, we think."

Lowering her eyes and drooping her shoulders despondently, the 'White Sheep' confessed.
Before the suspicious Subaru and the others, she held guilt and self-reproach in her eyes,

"When we left the 'Beloved Children' and joined up with the 'Silver Foxes' like this, there were many chances to trip up the opponent's plans. So we think Mama realized it too. —That 'Six Tongues' had gotten on her tail."

"Well, if there's a traitor in your own ranks, it's natural to think so... Or is it that? Capella, once someone leaves her side, she forgets and never thinks of them again?"

"No! If anything, she's the type of person who remembers it forever."

"I knew it! Consistent characterization there. Seriously, what a nasty piece of work..."

His understanding of Capella's twisted personality was reinforced once again, and Subaru spat that out. As if to supplement the exchange with the 'White Sheep', Russell raised another finger,

"As she says, the enemy likely knew our hand was becoming stronger. When the Witch's Cult attacked Priestella en masse, the reason 'Lust', who had never appeared openly before, brazenly showed herself was likely to make us aware of her existence."

"Aware of her existence... What's the point of doing that?"

"—'Six Tongues' has already killed seven people who were supposedly Capella Emerada Lugunica."

"What?"

"It's a fact. Whenever there was an eyewitness report matching the appearance of 'Lust' confirmed in Priestella, we had no choice but to move to verify it. Naturally, in the meantime, other schemes using the 'Beloved Children' were also enacted. This current affair is my fault for being too spread thin dealing with those."

"...Needless to ask, but those seven were imposters, I suppose?"

"Yes. Needlessly to say."

Russell explained unemotionally, simply stating that he had been outmaneuvered. But if Subaru were in his position, he couldn't imagine being able to keep from raging in fury.
Was even that rampage in Priestella, which spawned so many tragedies, merely a preparatory move for Capella to later toy with 'Six Tongues' and seize control of the Kingdom?
Destroying and twisting the lives of so many people.

"—!"

"...Subaru, I understand how you feel, but calm down, I suppose. You're only hurting yourself."

"Huh? Oh, sorry. I just..."

As Subaru gritted his teeth and hung his head, Beatrice, sitting in his lap, pressed her back against his chest. What she gently touched was Subaru's right arm, where he had unconsciously been digging in his nails.
Looking, the handkerchief that had been wrapped around the burn he got at the McMahon mansion was removed and replaced with a clean bandage. Over that bandage, he had been about to dig his left nails in again. About to apologize for that unconscious action, he suddenly noticed something. —The pain from the burn was completely gone.

"Was this you, Russell-san... no, 'White Sheep'-chan?"

"Eh? Ah, that's not me. That was 'Blue Snake'-san's..."

"'Blue Snake'?"

"—One of my subordinates. A skilled healer. Forgive my presumption, but we treated all your injuries while you were asleep. Is there any discomfort?"

"Ah, yeah, none. So none it's almost uncomfortable."

He lightly rotated his wrist and swung his arm, and it felt exactly like it was in perfect condition.
Even considering his mana shortage, to be able to heal a burn that Beatrice's power could only manage first-aid for, Russell's subordinates seemed to be quite the capable group.
If surface wounds were healed, then Crusch's and Rachins's should be healed too.
Though—

"—My old man."

With a hand to his mouth, Rachins, lost in thought, wasn't in a state to care about that right now.
If it was true that Capella's influence had extended to the Royal Castle and that the senior nobles, starting with the 'Sage Council', had been replaced, then Rachins's father was likely among them.
While Rachins often showed rebellious feelings towards his father, the unexpected intelligence he occasionally glimpsed seemed to have a solid core rooted in his upbringing.
And it was likely that his father wasn't unrelated to that core.

"Rachins, you alright?"

"...I just got stripped half-naked. What's there to be?"

"—. I see. Got it."

Subaru respected Rachins's answer, even though he probably understood the intent of the question.
It was only natural to be worried. And at this moment, Subaru had no way to resolve it, and Rachins didn't seem to want to share what was in his heart.
The feeling of worrying about one's family is heavy. From experience, he couldn't say that talking about it would make it easier, so he couldn't force it. Of course, if he wanted to talk, Subaru would listen—

"—Oii oii, are you done with that gloomy, tiresome talk yet?"

—Bashing in that delicate atmosphere, the infirmary door was violently opened.
The one who stomped in with insolent footsteps was a dangerous figure in black clothes and a jester's mask—the 'Black Dog', carrying a large bag in one hand.
Since Subaru and the others were safe, he assumed this one was too, but,

"Way to interrupt. We're in the middle of an important talk here."

"Goodness me, aren't you the busy bee. I bet you're the type to say there's not a single instant where you aren't having an important talk, since you're living so desperately!"

"'Black Dog', stop it! Natsuki Subaru-san is our benefactor!"

"Ooh, actin' all goody-goody. You're a wicked woman who's skilled at making others wag their tails, yet here you are, not wagging your own enough—instead of your head hanging, seems your ass is hanging low! Kuhahaha!"

"Ugh—!"

Scolded by the 'Black Dog's' rudeness, the 'White Sheep' turned red in the face at his counterattack.
It seemed these two, despite both having left the 'Beloved Children', didn't share a closely trusting relationship like Subaru and Beatrice.
Of course, Subaru was inclined to side with the 'White Sheep'—

"That's enough unnecessary chatter, 'Black Dog'. Be brief."

"Tch, I'm here to say, the preparations for moving are almost ready, so all you fine folks should get ready too, da!"

"Woof!"

"Uwah, what the—!?"

Speaking roughly, the 'Black Dog' suddenly hurled the large bag he was carrying at Subaru and the others. Subaru and Beatrice instinctively pulled back as it landed at their feet, on the bed.
As the 'White Sheep' hurriedly opened the mouth of the bag, what was inside—

"—Robes with a 'Perception Obstruction' effect. We obtained them through Roswaal. There are ones for Natsuki-dono, Beatrice-dono, and also for Crusch-sama. Ah, and a spare for Rachins-dono as well."

"Thanks for the afterthought!"

While Rachins, treated as an extra, spat that out, Subaru raised an eyebrow at the phrase 'Perception Obstruction' he hadn't heard in a while, and spread the robe on Beatrice's lap.
It was white fabric. Subaru couldn't tell by touching it, but Beatrice nodded, "Mm,"

"It's definitely something Roswaal had a hand in, I suppose. This adds credibility to the story that the bearded man is Roswaal's friend, in fact."

"You say that like it's unfortunate news... Well, as wanted fugitives, we're grateful for these robes, but did you say we're moving? Isn't this the 'Six Tongues' hideout?"

"No, this is merely one of several small safe houses. It's insufficient for opposing the current 'Beloved Children' forces... We'll be abandoning it shortly."

"But that's... No, you guys understand the enemy's scariness far better than we do, Russell-san. We're just along for the ride; sorry. I'll follow your instructions."

Just when they thought they'd finally settled, they were told to move again immediately. Subaru reflexively started to object, but quickly withdrew his protest.
The enemy's fearsomeness and meticulousness had been more than sufficiently explained. Without having met up with Russell and the others, they'd likely still be chased by unseen enemies even now.
So Subaru decided to follow Russell's judgment here.

"Then, do we move right away? Or rather, is the next place we're moving to far from here?"

"Yes, it will take some time. —After all, we will be leaving the Royal Capital."

"...Eh?"

Unable to fully swallow the explanation that hit his eardrums, Subaru's eyes widened.
Hoping it was some kind of misunderstanding, he waited for Russell to say different words, but contrary to Subaru's expectations, Russell's expression remained unchanged.
Naturally, Subaru had no choice but to take time and digest those words—

"—I can't easily agree, I suppose. The way you're talking just now, it sounds like Emilia in the castle gets left behind, in fact."

"Yes. If I may speak without fear of misunderstanding, we also cannot spare the effort to meet up with the members of your camp who are fleeing the Royal Capital. We are already within the enemy's grasp. If we don't move before that hand closes and the gaps disappear, it will be irrecoverable."

"That... even so..."

"I'll say it again. We are abandoning this base and escaping the Royal Capital. By now, this city is a demon's den ruled by the 'Beloved Children'. —We cannot be allowed to face defeat."

—At Russell's refusal of defeat, his voice filled with strong resolve and pride, Subaru was at a loss for words.

"— —"

Subaru's understanding was naive. Shallow. Insufficient.
The situation was even worse than Subaru imagined; they were on the verge of losing—unwittingly placed on the executioner's block, the moment of their beheading close at hand. That's likely what it meant.

But—

"Subaru, Subaru, look at Betty, I suppose. Betty is here, I suppose."

Beatrice, who had turned around, hugged the trembling Subaru from the front. The sensation of her small hands stroking his back reminded Subaru how to breathe, something he had forgotten.

"Russell-san, I get your point. I get it. But Emilia..."

Leave the Royal Capital, fallen into enemy hands. Refuse defeat. Create an opportunity to fight back.
He understood the intent. He understood the logic. The Royal Capital was nothing but dangerous now, and unless they made a bold move, they'd be playing into the enemy's hands. —Leaving Emilia behind in that place? Giving up on reuniting with their scattered comrades? Running away?

Was that a choice Natsuki Subaru could—

"—'White Sheep'."

"...! Yes."

Before Subaru, lost in thought and embracing Beatrice, Russell suddenly called the 'White Sheep'. At that call, the 'White Sheep' faltered for a moment, then nodded.
Then she stepped up to the bedside and gently held Subaru's hand in both of hers.

"'White Sheep'-chan...?"

"I understand your feelings, painfully so. The decision to be separated from someone precious is heart-rendingly painful. But, you wouldn't say 'Then let's die together'... right?"

"— —"

"Please believe in us. With the power of Duchess Karsten and Natsuki Subaru-san here, we will surely not lose. I beg you... please..."

Desperately, her eyes trembling as if on the verge of tears, the 'White Sheep' persuaded Subaru.
It was a platitude, an idealistic theory, the same stock conclusion Subaru had repeated to himself ten, a hundred times to convince himself. —And yet, for some reason, hearing it from the 'White Sheep's' mouth moved his heart.

"—Russell-san. The ones in the castle—Emilia and the others?"

"The enemy will likely refrain from harming the royal selection candidates. Even if they're subjected to restrictions, their personal safety won't be violated. I have collaborators keeping watch."

Taking a deep breath and exhaling, Subaru asked, and Russell answered.
The response, clearly intended to alleviate Subaru's worries as much as possible, was likely the maximum consideration and concession Russell could offer.

Emilia's safety relied on the enemy's conscience. The safety of their comrades relied on their individual strength. —Given the opponent, it was undeniable that these were all poor bets.

Even so—

"—I will definitely save Emilia. And everyone else too. Remember that."

Even as he felt his whole body burning with the dark flames seething deep in his chest, he made his resolve.
At Subaru's answer, Beatrice stiffened, and the 'White Sheep', still holding his hand, let out a faint sigh. Watching silently, Rachins, catching Russell's glance, stuck his tongue out as if to say he was clearly dissatisfied but wouldn't object.

Only one person, the 'Black Dog', leaning his back against the wall and touching his masked face—

"—Kuhah, go drop dead, you bastard."

—He muttered that at no one in particular, full of spite, the words falling to the floor of the medicine-scented room and fading away.
